name duel-doctrine-mig-1
timeout 600

# THE ASYMMETRIC DUEL, GEOMETRY 7 — THE FIRST DECIDED DUEL: THE MiG FLIES ITS OWN DOCTRINE. Identical to duel-headon.fbm in
# every respect but two lines of PILOT VARIANT (pilot/FBPilotTuning, `doc/missions/combat.md`) on the
# MiG — no code differs, and the F-16 is the same default pilot it is everywhere else in the campaign.
#
# WHY THE DEFAULT DOCTRINE IS WRONG FOR THIS WEAPON, and it is an argument off the two launch zones
# rather than a preference. Both pilots ship with `InterceptShotRtrFactor` = 1.0: shoot at Rtr, the
# range from which the round arrives EVEN IF THE TARGET TURNS AND RUNS. For an AIM-120 that is exactly
# right — the shooter is free the moment the seeker takes over, so waiting for the no-escape range
# costs nothing. For an R-27R it is close to the worst rule available:
#
#   [MESS, duel-headon] R-27R  Raero 39.2 nm   Rtr 10.3 nm     AIM-120  Raero 31.1 nm   Rtr 9.8 nm
#
# The MiG carries the LONGER kinematic reach and the SHORTER no-escape range, and it has to point at
# the target for the whole time of flight either way (weapons.md, FBSeekerHandoverS = -1). Closing to
# Rtr therefore buys it nothing it can use and costs it the 40 s during which the F-16 walks into its
# own trigger. Launching at 1.4 x Rtr spends the reach it actually has: the round is defeatable by a
# cold turn, and a cold turn is a fighter that is no longer attacking.
#
# THE TWO LINES ARE COUPLED AND THE COUPLING IS PHYSICAL: a shot cannot be taken from further out than
# the lock it is guided on, so `pilot_lock_nm` moves with `pilot_shot_rtr`. 16 nm is the N019's own
# 27 nm search reach less the margin a manoeuvring target needs, the same construction the default
# 13.5 uses one ladder step lower.
#
# READING RULE (PRE-2026-07-29): exit 1 with fulcrum SUCCESS. This is THE decided duel in the MiG's
# direction, and the campaign needs it: without it the table would say the F-16 dominates, when what it
# dominates is a MiG flying the F-16's doctrine. MEASURED — see doc/duels.md for the full debriefing.
#
# RE-MEASURED 2026-07-29 after the spawn-tick frame fix (doc/sensors.md 10, item 24). THE DECISION SAT
# INSIDE THE R-27R's FUZE RADIUS: closest approach 9.35 -> 13.22 m against a 13.8 m fuze. The round still
# detonates, the damage no longer kills, and the exit moves 0 -> 3 (both alive at the timeout). The
# doctrine lever still does what the file claims — the MiG shoots first, from further out, and holds the
# viper defensive — but this arena no longer DECIDES, and a campaign that needs a decided MiG win has to
# say so with a geometry rather than with 4 m of burst distance.

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.40000 8000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim9
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 8.40000 8000 450
  objective kill unit fulcrum
  objective survive

unit fulcrum
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 46.90000 7.85000 8000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set pilot_shot_rtr 1.4                   # spend the Raero this weapon has instead of its Rtr
  set pilot_lock_nm 16                     # ...which needs the designation to reach that far out
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 5.85000 8000 450
  objective kill unit viper
  objective survive
